## How to write them

One test per claim in the feature's story and metrics. Walk the pattern's steps the way the person does and assert the success signal: the observable that says the person got the value. Make real what has to be real for the test to mean anything. Take no shortcut the person cannot take. Assert nothing the unit tests already assert. Delete tests this feature invalidates.

Before writing each test, imagine the feature working and worthless: the data loads but is wrong, the run starts but never finishes. A test that still passes asserts an intermediate, not the value.

## What to produce

`acceptance_tests`: one row per test: `{ claim, signal, drives, real, faked, file }`.

`responses`: nothing on a first pass.

